From 314b9448d34cdaf449092008e4d373731d1f2655 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:47:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/46] net: realtek: r8169soc: support the RTD1395

Support the RTD1395 Ethernet port with its embedded 10/100 PHY.
One kernel now serves the RTD1295, the RTD1296 and the RTD1395.
The OF match data selects the SoC at run time.
The new compatible is "realtek,rtd1395-r8168".
"Realtek,r8168" keeps the RTD129x behaviour.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig    |   5 +-
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169soc.c | 822 +++++++++++++++---------
 2 files changed, 517 insertions(+), 310 deletions(-)

